# safety.meridian
# Flat-path regression coverage for the Phase-8 rule desugar (top-of-file
# rules, no headings). The same rule shapes now express in-section inside
# corpora/clinical/skills/*.meri (medicationadminister.meri, dosecheck.meri,
# dischargereview.meri, vitalsmonitor.meri) — this fixture keeps the original
# flat path exercised too. See docs/13_SKILL_MD_PORTING.md and AGENTS.md §6
# pitfall #15.

# Rules

A medication order with allergy check "conflict" must not be administered.

A nurse may administer medication orders whose dose count is at most 2.

A high risk medication order must be approved by an attending before administration.

When a patient is flagged as unmonitored, escalate the patient.

# Workflows

To let a nurse administer a medication order:
  invoke medication.administer with order = the medication order.

To have an attending approve the administration of a medication order:
  invoke audit.log with order = the medication order.

To escalate an unmonitored patient:
  invoke patient.escalate with patient = the patient.
